```console
$ useful workflow run release --help
Free an ended run's subject, on this machine or in Cloud

Usage: useful workflow run release [OPTIONS] <RUN>

Arguments:
  <RUN>  Run directory, run ID or subject

Options:
      --json                   Print the workflow result as JSON
      --org <ORG>              Organization ID or exact slug to act in (default: USEFUL_ORG, then the project of this checkout, then your only organization)
      --api-key-file <PATH|->  Authenticate with a service API key from a private file, or - for standard input
      --allow-insecure-http    Allow this command's Useful Machinery requests over insecure HTTP connections
  -h, --help                   Print help

RUN is a run directory, a run ID or a subject. An ID or a subject is looked up under the useful home and, when the home holds no such run, in Cloud in the organization in effect.

The command applies to an ended run. A run under the home that has not ended is refused, and the refusal names the commands that apply; Cloud refuses the release of a live Cloud run.

For a run under the home the command records the release, which frees the run's subject for a new run.

For a Cloud run the command asks Cloud, as an organization owner, to release the run's subject claim under one request key, sent again if the response is lost.

```
